  "extraNote": "the Joomla contract's first three palettes (the template's T3 less variables and Bootstrap 3's) and the white card surface: the carried source sheets are the Joomla 1.0.6 sheets, tokenized with those palettes, so the same colours are the ones they read the slot for",
  "selectors": {
    "display": "h1.wp-block-heading.hero-heading, .tracy-display",
    "heading": ["main h2.wp-block-heading"],
    "buttonPrimary": [
      ".tracy .btn-primary:not(.btn-decor):not(.wp-block-button)",
      ".tracy .wp-block-button.btn-primary > .wp-block-button__link",
      ".tracy a.btn.btn-lg:not(.btn-decor):not(.btn-default.btn-block)"
    ],
    "button": [".tracy .btn:not(.btn-decor):not(.wp-block-button)", ".tracy .wp-block-button__link"],
    "bodyFace": ["body.tracy"],
    "section": [".tracy main .t3-section"],
    "card": [".tracy-card"],
    "pill": [".label"]
  },
  "selectorsNote": "the theme keeps the source's class names (t3-*, acm-*, btn), so the buttons are Bootstrap's .btn as on the Joomla contract; the decorated split buttons (.btn-decor) keep the template's padding, size and type for the same reason as there (a label box beside an arrow cell drawn on its right padding)",
  "contrast": {
    "accent-text": "main a:not([class*=btn]):not(:has(img))",
    "body": "main p",
    "heading": "body :is(h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)",
    "text": "body :is(p, li, a, span, small, label, td, th, dd, dt, blockquote, figcaption, button)",
    "block-text": "body div:not(:has(> :is(div, p, ul, ol, section, article, header, footer, nav, main, aside, figure, table, form, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6)))"
  },
  "ready": true,
  "readyNote": "measured 22/10/2026 on the release of 1.0.1 (pack restored from the release folder, flow.mjs with the 15 featured systems at 1440 and 390, native and derived side; design-system-measurement.json of 1.0.1): 60 of 60 rows pass, CON-1 and MODE-2 included (1.0.0: 59 of 60, the row left was Airbnb derived dark at 390, the hero heading half on the accent bar, 2.92 < 3.0). Fixed by DECISIONS D-30 (b): under a system the heading's accent bar reads bg and the dark-side heading is plain fg; unworn the computed style is the same as 1.0.0. 22/10/2026, TDSR round on 1.0.1: the 14 must-fix rules the preview exposed are answered from this contract (followRules and sideRules as on joomla-ja-restaurant.json, the logo kept light on the dark side, DECISIONS D-36 and D-37); preview measured on all 31 pages at light and dark, 0 must-fix; GROUND-2 and BORDER-1 fixed from this contract (D-38): TDSR 0 FAIL on 1.0.1.",
