  "sideNote": "Bootstrap 3's status components (alerts, panels, labels, the info button, table states) carry the template's literal pale grounds and status words, as on the Joomla contract (joomla-ja-restaurant.json sideRules, the same rules: the theme keeps the source's class names): they read the status roles under a system. Dark side, no dark logo set (D-36): the customer's own logo picture stays and is drawn light on the dark ground instead of the name in words, so the mark keeps its size and content (IDENT-1); with a dark logo set nothing changes.",
  "followNote": "the same follow rules as the Joomla contract (text the template sets white in one rule on an accent fill set in another, the secondary and inverse buttons, the category chips), minus the hero bar (D-30: the theme reads bg itself) and the owl slideshow ground.",
  "literalsNote": "#333333 is the template's own ink on its own fixed light swatch (.swatch-item.color-gray-lighter, a #eeeeee sample box of the style guide page): the box is a colour sample whose ground no system repaints, so its words keep dark ink under every system. the first happy-hours description (.acm-happyhours.style-1 .hp-desc) keep the template's own #3a352f under every system: dark words with a white text shadow on a light photograph, which no system ground is under (preview probe v10 20/10/2026: the system's text read 1.68:1 on the photo under Moxie)"
